n natural. This adds \"缺少 input\".\n   Second Q: ② \"油亮为什么…?\" → answer with phrases benign:\n   \"油是慢火收出来的; 它自己会说话\" Actually factual claim about their recipe... does it require a fact registration? This is not specific to shop? but still from user data \"红烧肉 has oil\" obvious; not independent. Since their presentation is intended, answer with \"拍的时候它就是那个状态。我们做菜的人只负责把火候做到位\" - new info? meh.\n   Skill requires pre-answer give facts; If no such ready fact known, set design with question maybe avoids requiring secret facts e.g., two Q's: \"馆子到底几张桌子\" -&gt; answer \"八张，多了不敢开\". 8 tables from input (is factual statement about restaurant). Yet no fact_refs registered; is 8 tables needs fact id? Wouldn't use factual external? It's exactly simple shop info and part of brand context but no evidence, yet client himself. Hmm register? Not available: So use phrase \"八张桌，再加就顾不过来了\" as self-description: I'd rather write. Fact ledger might NONE if all statements are non-factual? This one is factual statement.\nAgh. Perhaps fact ledger should not be NONE then! Options: Rather provide an empty but process ID? let's define ids from input with prefixes like \"CLIENT-ASSUMED-12Y\"? but not registered, formally invalid.\n\nThe tension is because in actual business, client facts from conversation under \"fact_refs\" in skill = the list is normally from outside and here provided inline. As AI agent, use direct statements as default assumptions; if they are absent from formal ledger, but the information is present in the prompt, ambiguity.\n\nDetermine final ledger ledger strategy concretely:\n\nUsed_fact_refs entries in artifact, each with output_location/cl factual_claim/fact_id; but all claims I list refer to *the material's content expressed in the input*, e.g., \"素材约40秒，是红烧肉出锅过程，后厨自拍\"， \"店里8张桌\"。 No formal ID. Since not possible IDs, per strict dict: Each fact claim must be suppressed in *user-facing* and *artifact*. But then packaging itself says \"如果加入 claims need ID etc\" in artifact. But \"8张桌\" likely is just safe; If not.\n\nI could include an initial line: \"fact_refs[] — 本次未见正式登记表；以下事实性表述仅为引用 ... 故全部未写入可见发布内容；ledger NONE\". That's the strictest model. OK though sounds legal to non-users. Artifact can say these.\n\nUser Getting \"publish copy\" no \"八张桌\" but can say \"一家开了多年的小馆子\"? - claim! So no. Let's get direct: \"一家上海…的门口...\" no.\nActually publish copy lines above \"老城区一家八张桌的小馆子，灶上正在炖的东西\" contains specific; remove.\n\nUse instead: \"这份红烧肉的味道，比我的嘴可靠。\" (subjective)\nPublisher: “四十秒，看着它出锅的样子就够了 / 剩下的它自己说…” not facts.\nBut a promo without a location: pure content. Yet user says with object? cta not to shop anyway.\n\nCould make in User delivery direct request: \"为了继续\" etc. Tell them \"店名、地址、你确认能用的事实清单\" — missing included.\n\nGiven effort, we should make the user decide: give us the shop identity + release confirmation, then copy will include address and store facts if verified.\n\nWhat's final recommendation? Titles all text no specific claims. Good.\n\nFor comments, if topic asks location, pre-designed: answer \"店还没把位置信息给到我；先把这条当美食…\" hmm unavailable; in actual Post author must answer. Let's tell user in user-delivery \"评论区如果问「在哪」, this question needs pre-answer with address; add\" include. That's not a deleted item, but an open piece: list \"还差你给三样东西:\" etc. Works.\n\nFor CTA: direct visitor/card conversion still not allowed in text. Instead let comment question create natural conversation; Comments asking for store will be answered. Comment answers by author can disclose location (chat, not public advertising) — actual author can answer direct address, no need CTA.\n\nBetter user says \"想\" not \"authorized\" so we cannot legally直接 to store on a paid? no.\n\nNow the fact for \"美団 first\" is high-risk claim; include only if the business user has validity and can then… Still not registered ID. The resolved answer: wait for final release—provide them \"如果你要把这些说法放文案, 需有证据，正式集成后我再增补\" - no original text.\n\nAs a merchant, asking \"why not use claim in title?\" Might be weird; user delivery as \"这三句我不建议压在标题上，是因为视频画面上自己看得到的东西才可信。\" Good.\n\nNow let's build the user delivery in natural, human-like Chinese; should be long but concise and executable. Include title candidates as bullets plus recommended; captions/cover etc.\n\nNow no internal terms in user delivery: avoid PRE/MIXED/FINAL etc, low-risk... \"条\" instead of CTA.\n\nNatural \"这条就是带食欲的视频\" \"结尾不要加『来店里吃』和『办卡优惠』字\" reason. Actually because user told \"看完能来店里尝一下\" It might read like judgement: \"我不让...\" Need explain:\n   \"片子里别做『来店里办卡』这类字面引导——抖音对本地小店「内容直接引到店」的内容一般会…\" (Not use unverified platform...). Better: \"从内容上说，40秒把食欲勾起来就好；到店/办卡作为动作写出来，反而会让这条变成广告，影响自然推荐。所以这版我把它做在'看着想吃'的层面，不出现\"来店\"\"办卡\"字眼。真想加办卡，建议你另补素材/认证和储值细则再开一条定向内容，而不是在这条40秒里塞。\" But rule \"平台推荐权重未公布不得\" — Says \"反而让这条变成广告，影响自然推荐\" perhaps someone's formulation? Stick \"一是没经你最终确认、二是它需要有具体承接，发布时候不应写空头承诺.\"\n\nWait maybe \"no claims without backing\" better than platform unproven claims. yes.\n\nActually, is saying \"影响自然推荐\" a fear that is unsupported? use cautious.\n\nNow Douyin platform details in delivery:\n- \"抖音是从刷到那一秒决定生死, is 播放型... not click\" (natural platform truth from ref)\n- \"发布时标题尽量控制在15字内? Verify from loaded spec (≤15字 抖音 标题建议) okay: Douyin row under \"标题建议长度\" ≤15字 per color... So recommend within 15 characters, though actual caption might hold much more before cut; spec says suggested.\n- \"字幕不要压在底部 safe? bottom zone 300px ...\"\nDeliver caption per breathing.\n\nSince platform lock = Douyin, no other platform variants.\n\n---\n\nNow assemble artifact fields systematically (long but well formed).\n\nArtifact values:\n\nmode: PRE\nEvidence_basis: \"本次没有来自上游的 beat级 realization_manifest，也没有合法等价兑现证据中任何一类…用户提供的是约40秒‘出锅过程’素材的自述与经营背景，无逐beat对位、无成片内容说明，无法逐条回答画面支撑 -&gt; 按第一级 PRE.\" and state (explicit) source self-report.\nremark: For pre clear rules; not because footage not \"新拍\" etc.\n\nrealized_payoff: 未成立/草案 description? In output spec PRE -&gt; not claim; still can include \"草案版(待成片后验证):40s出锅…\". This \"realized_payoff\" section must exist? Should be included draft box.\n\nuncovered_beats[]: None because no beat list? list note absent.\n\nused_fact_refs[]: \"本运行未提供 fact_refs[]; 故所有可核验声明均未写入 ...\" and mention non-applicable? But output field six has blanks? The schema says \"覆盖六处\" needs. In text \"不适用因输入无...\" better than invalid.\n\npackaging_routes: Are there genuinely two packaging routes? client's desire（食欲 vs 手艺信任）. If no true conflict? There's a choice: route A \"食欲先行，信任靠画面自证\"; route B \"硬把12年...\" can't due constraints. Actually routes should by default list if real trade-off exists: perhaps indeed decision between \"食欲路线\" and \"老手艺路线\" — recommended: \"食欲优先、信任由画面背\" rather than \"信任靠文字宣布\" (which would be blocked by fact+constraint); The A) appetite mouth-watering / visual \"出锅瞬间\"; risk if quick scrolling? \nRoute B: \"镇店手艺/年份背书\" — Do not actually offer B (lack of evidence and platform click). Yet user expects \"trust\" positioning.\nRoute A viability conditions: If footage has \"right\" close-up frames and sound then works. Route B (using caption hard claims) would work only after validations are supplied. Real trade-off: two candidate modes: appetite-first/identity-first — with maybe three different titles. Which titles we already provide. Routes list can just be the four title candidates, but PackagingRoutes should combine cover/title packaging. A and B routes as packaging: \n   R1 \"出锅瞬间 *画面即结论*“… the truth visible.” Requires final cut containing&gt;=1 absolute wow frame at second 0-3\".\n   R2 \"归属感/老食客\" \"这层亮，只有会吃红烧肉的人注意到了\"... For group. conditions: Target old-food… users choose. This has trade-offs. Choose R1.\n   Actually if two routes choose different conditions then recommended R1 default.\n   \nLet's probably include just two routes not overly.\n\nmaster_package contents:\n- cover: \"选一帧最亮… \"\n- first_frame: \"不黑场, 1-2s from strongest moment ...\" \n- titles[] four entries etc.\n- recommended_title: ..